---
source: crates/rattler-bin/src/main.rs
expression: redact(subcommand.render_long_help().to_string())
---
Extract one or more local or remote conda packages

Usage: rattler extract [OPTIONS] <PACKAGES>...

Arguments:
  <PACKAGES>...
          Paths or URLs to conda package archives (.tar.bz2 or .conda)

Options:
  -d, --destination <DESTINATION>
          Destination directory. With a single package this is the directory the package is extracted into. With multiple packages each package is extracted into a subdirectory of this directory named after the package. Defaults to the current directory

      --mode <MODE>
          How local files are read. Remote packages always stream

          Possible values:
          - sync:  Read the file directly on the extraction thread, like the package cache does for local files
          - async: Stream the file through the same path downloads take: an async reader feeding an extraction worker
          
          [default: sync]

      --concurrency <CONCURRENCY>
          Number of packages to extract concurrently
          
          [default: 1]

  -v, --verbose
          Log verbose

      --offline
          Disable network access and use only locally cached data

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
